<title>FRANCE: France's Chirac to address U.N. meeting in June.</title>
<headline>France's Chirac to address U.N. meeting in June.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>French President Jacques Chirac will address a U.N. General Assembly session on rural development on June 23, government spokesman Alain Lamassoure said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Lamassoure said the U.N. meeting in New York would follow a summit of the G7 group of leading industrialised nations in Denver, Colorado, which will include environment as one of its major themes.</p>
</text>
